<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tsutsujigasaki Castle</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1519</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tsutsujigasaki was the fortified residence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/takeda-clan">Takeda clan</a> in Kai Province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, built by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/takeda-nobutora">Takeda Nobutora</a> in 1519 in what became the town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kofu">Kōfu</a>. It was the seat of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/takeda-shingen">Takeda Shingen</a> and was abandoned after his son Katsuyori moved to the new Shinpu Castle in 1581. The Takeda Shrine now stands on the site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tsutsujigasaki-castle.jpg" alt="Tsutsujigasaki Castle" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 前田左衛門佐 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E8%BA%91%E8%BA%85%E3%83%B6%E5%B4%8E%E9%A4%A8.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
